    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0587" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/614: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marriner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-04-04T19:00:00-05:00">April 4, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. For Norman Davis. For your information, the discussions now under way here
                    with the British representatives are already turning in the direction of your
                    second alternative.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d357-f1"/> The British Ambassador and
                    I have already tentatively agreed to invite from time to time representatives of
                    other nations to join informally in our current discussions of world economic
                    questions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="36" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 71, April 3, from the Chargé in Great Britain, <ref
                        target="#pg482">p. 482</ref>.</p>
            </note>
